$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):PRO(1):YIELD
$DATUM 92
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAT(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 934389-92-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedures for Borylation of Terminal Alkynes: Complex 1 (0.0025
mmol or 0.005 mmol) was placed in a vial and cold pinacolborane (3 mmol)
and toluene (3 ml, if applicable) were added. The resulting suspension
was stirred for five minutes at room temperature to get a clear yellow
solution, which was again cooled (ca. -15 °C). To this solution, cold
alkyne (2.5 mmol) was added dropwise over a period of 15 min under
stirring and the reaction mixture was allowed to stir at room
temperature. Progress of the reaction was monitored by GC analysis and
the products were isolated by column chromatography over silica gel using
ethyl acetate/hexane mixture as eluent.
2-[(Z)-2-phenylethenyl]-4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane3,
colorless oil, yield 92%. IR (DCM): 2981, 1619, 1422, 1373, 1316, 1254,
1140, 965, 883, 847, 809, 692 cm-1. 1HNMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.45 (d, J
= 7.3 Hz, 2H), 7.23-7.14 (m, 4H), 5.51 (d, J = 14.9 Hz, 1H), 1.20 (s,
12H). 13C-NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ 148.19 (CH), 138.51 (quat-C), 128.66
(CH), 128.05 (CH), 127.97 (CH), 83.51 (quat-C, OC), 24.84 (CH3). MS (ESI)
m/z 230.2 (M+, 71%), 215.2 (28%), 144 (87%), 129.2 (100%), 105.2 (59%),
86 (83%). HR/MS: calcd (C14H19O2B1)+ 230.1473. Found: 230.1475 .
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, stereoselective, alternative reaction conditions shown,
96:4 Z:E, no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ruthenium Catalyzed Hydroboration of Terminal Alkynes to Z-Vinylboronates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
