$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedures for Borylation of Terminal
Alkynes: Complex 1 (0.0025 mmol or 0.005 mmol) was placed in a vial and
cold pinacolborane (3 mmol) and toluene (3 ml, if applicable) were added.
The resulting suspension was stirred for five minutes at room temperature
to get a clear yellow solution, which was again cooled (ca. -15 °C). To
this solution, cold alkyne (2.5 mmol) was added dropwise over a period of
15 min under stirring and the reaction mixture was allowed to stir at
room temperature. Progress of the reaction was monitored by GC analysis
and the products were isolated by column chromatography over silica gel
using ethyl acetate/hexane mixture as eluent.
2-[(Z)-2-(6-methoxynaphthalen-2-yl)ethenyl]-4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane,
yellow flabby solid, yield 92%. IR (DCM): 3288, 3056, 2979, 2936, 2938,
1602, 1479, 1437, 1382, 1324, 1254, 1210, 1139, 1029, 965, 850, 673 cm-1.
1HNMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.03 (s, 1H), 7.85 (dd, J = 8.5, 1.6 Hz, 1H),
7.75 (t, J = 9.3 Hz, 2H), 7.45 (d, J = 14.9 Hz, 1H), 7.23 (dd, J = 9.0,
2.5 Hz, 1H), 7.14 (d, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H), 5.80 (d, J = 14.8 Hz, 1H), 3.89
(s, 3H), 1.40 (s, 12H). 13C-NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ 158.10 (quat-C,
ArCO), 148.61 (CH), 134.57 (quat-C, ArC), 134.09 (quat- C, ArC), 129.86
(CH), 128.78 (quat-C, ArC), 128.27 (CH), 127.25 (CH), 126.44 (CH), 118.99
(CH), 105.80 (CH), 83.55 (quat-C, OC), 55.23 (OCH3), 24.97 (CH3). MS
(ESI) m/z 323.3 ((M+1)+, 6%), 310.3 (M+, 5%), 183.2 (32%), 182.2 (100%),
167.1 (18%), 139.2 (91%), 84.1 (13%). HR/MS: calcd (C19H23O3B1)+
310.1735. Found: 310.1739.
