$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Labeling Experiment: Preparation of (Z)-C6H5CD=CHBpin. Complex 1 (0.005
mmol) was placed in a vial and cold pinacolborane (3 mmol) and toluene (3
ml) were added. The resulting suspension was stirred for five minutes at
room temperature to get a clear yellow solution, which was again cooled
(ca. -15 °C). To this solution, cold alkyne (2.5 mmol) was added dropwise
over a period of 15 min under stirring and the reaction mixture was
allowed to stir at room temperature. Progress of the reaction was
monitored by GC analysis and the products were isolated by column
chromatography over silica gel using ethyl acetate/hexane mixture as
eluent. Colorless oil, yield 90%. IR (DCM): 2978, 1609, 1575, 1495, 1370,
1328, 1244, 1141, 1110, 1007, 986, 961, 865, 843, 800 cm-1. 1H-NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.46-7.43 (m, 2H), 7.21-7.12 (m, 3H), 5.49 (d, J = 1.1 Hz,
1H), 1.17 (d, J = 2.1 Hz, 12H). 13C-NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ 147.86 (t, J
= 23.4 Hz, DC), 138.45 (quat-C), 128.69 (CH), 128.09 (CH), 128.00 (CH),
83.51 (quat-C, OC), 24.87 (CH3). MS (ESI) m/z 231 (M+, 89%), 216 (37%),
158 (16%), 145 (91%), 131 (100%). HR/MS: calcd (C14H18D1O2B1)+ 231.1536.
Found: 231.1535.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, stereoselective
