$DATUM Synthesis of (C6F5)2B(CH2CH2CH2CH(PPh3)CH2) (4) To a mixture suspension
of [HB(C6F5)2]n (100 mg, 0.29 mmol) and PPh3 (76 mg, 0.29 mmol) in
toluene (2.0 mL) was added 1,4-pentadiene (100 μL, 0.97 mmol). The
reaction was shaken until all was dissolved. The mixture was then let sit
at RT for 2 days, during which time a crystalline precipitate formed. The
mother liquor was decanted off, and the product was washed with toluene
(2.0 mL) followed by pentane (3 x 3.0 mL). The solid was dried in vacuo.
Yield: 177 mg, 90 %. The crystalline product was suitable for X-ray
diffraction studies. 4, yield 177 mg, 90 %. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD2Cl2, 298
K): δ 7.75 (m, 3H, para-Ph), 7.66-7.59 (m, 12H, ortho-Ph, meta-Ph), 3.16
(m, 1H, PCH), 2.05 (m, 1H, PCHCH2), 1.98 (m, 1H, PCHCH2CH2), 1.83 (m, 1H,
BCH2CHP), 1.76 (m, 1H, PCHCH2CH2), 1.56 (d, 1H, 2JHH = 13.6 Hz, BCH2CH2),
1.20 (m, 1H, PCHCH2), 0.71 (dt, 1H, 2JHH = 12.6 Hz, 3JHH = 12.6 Hz, 3JHP
= 3.8, BCH2CHP), 0.27 (dt, 1H, 2JHH = 13.1 Hz, 3JHH = 13.1 Hz, 3JHH =
3.7, BCH2CH2). 11B NMR (128 MHz, CD2Cl2, 298 K): δ -12.93 (s). 13C{1H}
NMR (101 MHz, CD2Cl2, 298 K): δ 149.41 (dm, 1JCF = 238 Hz, o-C6F5),
148.63 (dm, 1JCF = 236 Hz, o-C6F5), 138.49 (dm, 1JCF = 246 Hz, p-C6F5),
137.89 (dm, 1JCF = 244 Hz, p-C6F5), 137.42 (dm, 1JCF = 246 Hz, m-C6F5),
137.01 (dm, 1JCF = 240 Hz, m-C6F5), 134.78 (d, 4JCP = 2.9 Hz, p-Ph),
134.25 (d, 2JCP = 8.4 Hz, o-Ph), 130.48 (d, 3JCP = 11.7 Hz, m-Ph), 119.93
(d, 1JCP = 81.0 Hz, i-Ph), 33.75 (d, 1JCP = 34.6 Hz, PCH), 30.62 (d, 2JCP
= 2.4 Hz, PCHCH2), 27.90 (d, 3JCP = 16.5 Hz, PCHCH2CH2), 23.24 (br,
BCH2CHP, BCH2CH2). 19F NMR (376 MHz, CD2Cl2, 298 K): δ -132.68 (dd, 2F,
3JFF = 25 Hz, 4JFF = 8 Hz, o-C6F5), -134.31 (d, 2F, 3JFF = 25 Hz, 4JFF =
8 Hz, o-C6F5), -163.46 (t, 1F, 3JFF = 20 Hz, p-C6F5), -164.83 (t, 1F,
3JFF = 20 Hz, p-C6F5), -166.49 (m, 2F, m-C6F5), -167.18 (m, 2F, m-C6F5).
31P{1H} NMR (162 MHz, CD2Cl2, 298 K): δ 27.09 (s). Anal. Calcd. for
C35H24BF10P: C, 62.16; H, 3.58. Found: C, 61.90; H, 4.04 %.
