$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM An oven-dried vial was charged with CuCl (2 mg, 0.02 mmol, 10 mol%),
B2pin2 (56 mg, 0.22 mmol, 1.1 equiv) and ligand (11 mol%) and sealed with
a septum. The vial was connected to an argon-vacuum line, evacuated and
backfilled with argon (×3). THF (0.6 mL/0.2 mmol of 1) was added and the
mixture was stirred for 30 min at room temperature. A 0.2 M NaOtBu
solution in THF (50 μL, 0.1 mmol, 0.5 equiv) was added dropwise and the
dark brown solution was stirred for 10 min. The reaction mixture was
cooled at-78 °C for 10 min and the corresponding cyclopropene 1 (1.0
equiv) was added followed by methanol (32 μL, 0.8 mmol, 4 equiv). Then,
the reaction mixture was stirred overnight at-20 °C. Et2O and water were
added and the layers were separated. The aqueous phase was extracted with
Et2O (×3) and the combined organic layers were washed with saturated NaCl
solution, dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated. The crude product
was purified by flash column chromatography (0-10% Et2O/pentane).
Compound (±)-2a. Entry: 3, Yield: 90%, Catalyst: xantphos. dr: ≥98:2.
Time: 12h.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, optimization study, optimized on temperature, sealed
vial used, diastereomeric ratio 98:2, optimized on ligand
