$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM [C5H5B(CH2)5CH3]2YCl (2). A toluene solution of 1-hexene (453 mg, 5.38
mmol in 2 mL of toluene) was added to 1 (150 mg, 0.539 mmol) in 4 mL of
toluene. After stirring for 4 days at 75 °C, the reaction mixture was
filtered. Evaporation of the orange filtrate in vacuo left an orange oil,
which was extracted with 3×2mL of hexane. Removal of the solvent of the
extract. 2 as an orange oil (215 mg, 89% yield). 1H NMR (400 MHz, C6D6,
25 °C): δ 7.44 (dd, J H-H = 10.4 Hz, J H-H = 7.2 Hz, 4H, 3-/5-H), 7.00
(d, J H-H J H-H = 9.6 Hz, 4H, 2-/6-H), 6.20 (t, J H-H = 7.2 Hz, 2H, 4-H),
1.80-1.72 (m, 4H, B(CH 2)5CH3), 1.60-1.53 (m, 8H, B(CH 2)5CH3), 1.50-1.37
(m, 8H, B(CH 2)5CH3), 0.97 (t, J H-H = 7.2 Hz, 6H, B(CH2)5CH 3). 13C NMR
(100 MHz, C6D6, 25 °C): δ 141.8, 133.4, 112.2, 33.3, 32.5, 28.0, 23.2,
22.5, 14.5. 11B NMR (128 MHz, C6D6, 25 °C): δ 46.9. 89Y NMR (19.6 MHz,
C6D6, 25 °C): δ -21.4. Anal. Calcd (%) for C22H36B2ClY: C, 59.18; H,
8.13. Found: C, 57.99; H, 8.61.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
