$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4. Asymmetric Rhodium-Directed
anti-Markovnikov Regioselective Boracyclopentannulation General
Procedure: A 10 mL oven-dried Schlenk flask was charged with the
appropriate NHC-BH3 (0.125 mmol), [Rh(nbd)2]BF4 (2.5 mg, 6.2 μmol, 5
mol%) and (S)-Xylyl-MeO-BIPHEP (3.6 mg, 6.2 μmol, 5 mol%) under argon.
Then, dry degassed dichloromethane (1 mL) was added and the mixture was
stirred at room temperature under argon for 2 minutes. The crude product
was filtered through a short plug of silica gel using dichloromethane (10
mL) as eluent to give the desired cyclic NHC-borane. The title compound
was filtered through a short plug of silica gel using dichloromethane (10
mL) as eluent to give 2k in 89% yield as colorless oil. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3) δ (ppm) 0.80-2.50 (m, 2H), 2.34 (bs, 1H), 2.62 (dd, 1H, 2J = 14.1
Hz, 3J = 10.8 Hz), 3.07 (dd, 1H, 2J = 14.1 Hz, 3J = 5.1 Hz), 3.70 (dd,
1H, 2J = 11.1 Hz, 3J = 5.8 Hz), 3.98 (dd, 1H, 2J = 11.1, Hz, 3J = 8.3
Hz), 6.96 (d, 1H, 3J = 1.9 Hz), 7.13-7.19 (m, 1H), 7.24-7.33 (m, 5H),
7.37 (t, 1H, 3J = 7.5 Hz), 7.49 (t, 2H, 3J = 8.1 Hz), 7.74 (d, 2H, 3J =
7.5 Hz). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) 34.1(HMQC), 42.6, 55.6, 117.2,
120.3, 121.1, 125.1, 127.5, 128.0, 128.7, 129.5, 138.2, 144.7. 11B NMR
(128 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) -21.7 (t, 1JB-H = 90.3 Hz). HRMS (ES, [M+Na]+)
calcd for [C18H19BN2Na]+: 297.1533; found: 297.1536FT-IR (ATR) ν (cm-1)
3169 (w), 3143 (w), 3088 (w), 3052 (w), 3021 (w), 2923 (w), 2854 (w),
2303 (m), 2251 (m), 1597 (w), 1502 (s), 1447 (w), 1420 (w), 1351 (w),
1282 (w), 1232 (w), 1158 (w), 1067 (w), 1043 (w), 970 (w), 908 (w), 760
(w), 726 (s), 690 (s), 652 (w), 612 (w). HPLC: Enantiomeric excess was
determined by HPLC with a Chiralcel OD-3, Hexane/isopropanol 95/5, 1
mL/min, UV 254 nm et CD 254nm; rt (minor) = 21.6 min, rt (major)= 24.6
min; 9.3:90.7 er. [α]20 D: -7.8, c = 1, CHCl3.
